/**
 * Seylan Bank Kiosk | Location registry
 * -------------------------------------
 * Google Apps Script web app + Google Sheet that decides which tablet gets which
 * branch Sensor. Each location can be claimed by at most "Max tablets" devices
 * per APK build. A new APK (new build ID in the app's config) starts with every
 * location free again.
 *
 *   GET  ?action=locations&build=<id>             → locations with free / taken counts
 *   GET  ?action=status&build=<id>&device=<id>    → this device's existing claim, if any
 *   POST {action:'claim', build, location, device, deviceName, pin}
 *                                                  → claims a location (one-time PIN)
 *   POST {action:'unlock', build, device, pin}    → checks the kiosk exit PIN
 *
 * Each branch has one-time PINs, one per tablet it allows (PIN column of the
 * Locations sheet, generated by setupRegistry). A PIN sets up exactly one
 * tablet, ever: it is then replaced with a fresh one, and a PIN found in the
 * Claims history never works again. PINs live only in the sheet and the
 * script, never in the APK.
 *
 * To reset a tablet (e.g. set up for the wrong branch), tick "Released" on its
 * Claims row. The branch is free again and the tablet returns to the setup
 * screen on its next check. Keep the row: it is the PIN history.
 *
 * To stop the service at a branch, untick "Active" on its Locations row. Its
 * tablets stay set up but show "Service unavailable" instead of the Sensor,
 * and the branch can't be set up on new tablets. Tick it again to resume.
 *
 * To retire a whole APK build, untick "Active" on its row in the Builds sheet
 * (each build adds itself the first time a tablet uses it). Its tablets show
 * "This app version is no longer in use" and it can't set up tablets any more.
 *
 * The kiosk exit PIN (Script Properties → EXIT_PIN) opens the hidden admin
 * menu on a tablet (5 quick taps in the bottom-left corner) to unlock it.
 * setupRegistry creates one if it is missing.
 *
 * 5 wrong PINs lock a tablet out for 15 minutes. Locked-out tablets are listed
 * in the Lockouts sheet: delete a row to let that tablet try again at once.
 * Setup: see registry/README.md.
 */

var CONFIG = {
